1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:19,000
In this update of the 2026.0 version, the functions related to virtual models have been improved, making it easier and more convenient to modify and create virtual models, including the new hybrid transformation function. Let's take a closer look at these functions.

2
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:28,000
First of all, the hybrid transformation function allows you to freely adjust the body and facial expressions of virtual models with hybrid transformation data in the shell.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Hybrid transformation refers to the data created in the external 3D tool, which includes various body shapes and facial transformation values other than the default form.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
From this version, when you import the data into the shell, you only need to move the slider to see the changes in real time.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Currently, we support GLBGLTF and VRM format.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The future plan is to expand the support to more formats.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Let me show you the hybrid transformation function and how to change the body shape of the virtual image.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
I have added a virtual model containing various body data and put it on.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
In the main menu, select the virtual model and open the virtual model editor.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
And select the hybrid transformation from the label bar.

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
In the variable parameter list, you will see the adjustable shape keys.

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
If you move the slider, you can see the virtual model's body shape changes in real time.

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Open the simulation.

14
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The clothing will also shrink at the same time as the model body shape changes.

15
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
The hybrid transformation function supports a variety of modifications.

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Specifically, it depends on the data type contained in the basic virtual model.

17
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
This time, let's add a virtual model file containing facial expression data.

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Select import from the main menu, then select GLTF.

19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Select the file to save as a virtual model.

20
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Select the file to save as a virtual model.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Select the file to save as a virtual model.

22
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Select the file to save as a virtual model.

23
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Check the variable parameter list.

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
You will find that this virtual model includes more hybrid transformations than the previous model.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
And it has many different adjustable parts.

26
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You can hide the data fold of each different area.

27
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,159
because the facial expression data is pre-made in the external tool.

28
00:02:21,159 --> 00:02:23,560
You can adjust the slider

29
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:27,659
to observe extremely subtle changes in the virtual model expression.

30
00:02:27,659 --> 00:02:30,240
Click on the star icon.

31
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:32,900
You can set the usual items as collections.

32
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:35,560
By turning on the high-resolution collection in the upper right corner,

33
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:45,099
you can focus more on adjusting the required items.

34
00:02:45,099 --> 00:02:47,960
Click on all items again.

35
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:51,400
If you want to restore all values to the original state at once,

36
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:58,159
just click on the reset button.

37
00:02:58,159 --> 00:03:01,500
Next, let's take a look at the customized configuration process after the improvement.

38
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,659
Now you can store external documents containing binding information

39
00:03:04,659 --> 00:03:09,799
as ZACS documents with virtual models.

40
00:03:09,799 --> 00:03:12,500
The key is that the name of the joint set in the configuration

41
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,159
must be the same as the name of the virtual model

42
00:03:14,159 --> 00:03:15,039
that needs to be merged with the virtual model.

43
00:03:15,039 --> 00:03:15,060
The key is that the name of the joint set in the configuration must be the same as the virtual model.

44
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,400
The key is that the name of the joint set in the configuration must be the same as the virtual model.

45
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:22,759
Check the name of the virtual model joint point.

46
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:25,819
Select the virtual model in the main menu.

47
00:03:25,819 --> 00:03:28,900
Select the customized configuration and open the window.

48
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:32,199
I will add a hair file here.

49
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:34,000
Add the prepared file.

50
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,400
You will find that the name of the joint of the configuration hair

51
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,659
matches the name of the virtual model joint.

52
00:03:38,659 --> 00:03:43,199
Therefore, no additional steps are required to immediately merge with the virtual model.

53
00:03:43,199 --> 00:03:45,000
Select to bind in the basic part.

54
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
In the customized configuration window,

55
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,599
set the ratio and shrink chart as automatic.

56
00:03:50,599 --> 00:03:55,240
Then you can store it directly as a virtual model configuration file.

57
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:59,099
The stored file will be created in the ZACS file format.

58
00:03:59,099 --> 00:04:02,159
This is the custom configuration format for CLO.

59
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:04,199
You can easily use this method

60
00:04:04,199 --> 00:04:08,039
to customize the external virtual model and CLO virtual model.

61
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:22,939
We have also added a kind of cartoon effect type that can make your clothes and virtual models look like 2D cartoon effects.

62
00:04:22,939 --> 00:04:25,240
Double-click the virtual model to select it.

63
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:29,000
Then in the material options card of the property editor,

64
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:35,000
change the type to cartoon effect only 3D.

65
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:40,339
The selected virtual model and configuration will be converted to 2D cartoon style.

66
00:04:40,339 --> 00:04:43,000
Once the cartoon material type is switched,

67
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,439
a detailed option of the effect will appear at the bottom.

68
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:47,040
Let's take a quick look.

69
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:55,000
In the shadow part, you can choose the shadow color.

70
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,939
Increasing the strength will make the edge of the shadow sharper,

71
00:04:57,939 --> 00:05:02,399
and adjusting the flatness can change the range of the shadow.

72
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:05,000
Let's adjust the parameters to check the effect.

73
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,839
Finally, select a mode in the contour line part,

74
00:05:16,839 --> 00:05:19,000
and adjust the width value.

75
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,240
You can create a contour line,

76
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:24,399
and create a high-quality cartoon texture.

77
00:05:24,399 --> 00:05:27,699
For more detailed options on the cartoon effect material type,

78
00:05:27,699 --> 00:05:34,660
please visit the CLO official website.

79
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:36,439
Finally, from this version,

80
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:40,939
we support UV editing for CLO virtual models and external virtual models.

81
00:05:40,939 --> 00:05:42,480
From the main menu, start UV editor,

82
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:42,879
and then select the UV editor.

83
00:05:42,879 --> 00:05:42,980
Then, from the main menu, start UV editor,

84
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:48,879
and then select the UV editor.

85
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:50,160
In the vertical menu bar,

86
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:52,000
you can add UV display objects.

87
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,439
You can selectively check the UV stickers

88
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:56,060
or the UV stickers of the virtual model

89
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,740
or costume in the 3D window at the moment,

90
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:59,759
and UV display.

91
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:01,839
Open the virtual model display.

92
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:03,480
You can see all the UV stickers

93
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:12,879
of the virtual model in the interface.

94
00:06:12,879 --> 00:06:20,659
If you just want to check the sticker of the selected object,

95
00:06:20,659 --> 00:06:23,120
select the UV display object in the display object,

96
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,659
and only display this sticker in the interface.

97
00:06:24,659 --> 00:06:27,519
In this way, even if the screen content is very complex,

98
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:29,759
you can only select and place the required elements,

99
00:06:29,759 --> 00:06:31,560
thereby greatly simplifying the workflow.

100
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,719
The above covers the various improvements of virtual models in CLO,

101
00:06:33,719 --> 00:06:35,560
from mixed transformation to the fun-filled cartoon effect material.

102
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,000
We hope these new features will make your work easier and more pleasant.

